    {
      "id": "claim_b55e8286d6824bfdbddae682c47e8095",
      "statement": "test_process_image_supports_multiple_formats proves multi-format processing: EXIF-stamped JPG and TIFF are copied into output/2024/06/15, an EXIF-less PNG is still copied (date falls back to file ctime), the output JPG gains a 'RelativePath:' entry in its EXIF UserComment (verified with piexif.load), and the TIFF is copied but the test only asserts its existence rather than directly asserting the absence of a tag. This contradicts the README's 'designed for JPEG images' note; SUPPORTED_FORMATS in sortinfolder.py actually accepts .jpg, .jpeg, .png, .heic, .tiff, .tif, .bmp, .webp, and the tests are the authoritative source of truth on format support.",
