    {
      "id": "claim_a6f80a8c3c2b4770b025c32675c95de1",
      "statement": "CI is defined in .ci/ci.yaml: the image is built from .ci/test.Dockerfile (python:3.12-slim with Pillow, exifread, and piexif installed via pip, WORKDIR /workspace), and the unit check runs [\"python\", \"-c\", \"import sortinfolder\"] via execv without a shell. The unit check is deliberately minimal — it verifies only that the module imports cleanly (compiles, resolves imports, defines functions without raising), which is also why the test suite's function-level imports are safe: importing the module must be side-effect-free because the entry point is guarded by if __name__ == \"__main__\".",
